      "title": "Coupling and Cohesion Mental Model",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Coupling and Cohesion Mental Model",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Definitions",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "{blue:Coupling} = how much one module must ==know about or change with== another",
                "{green:Cohesion} = how closely a module's ==own parts belong together==",
                "Goal: ==low coupling== between modules, ==high cohesion== within one",
                "They **reinforce** each other: focused modules need fewer links"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. The Two Tests",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Coupling",
                "Cohesion"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Ask",
                  "Change A: how many other modules must change?",
                  "Job in one sentence: any 'and'?"
                ],
                [
                  "Bad",
                  "{red:Many ripples}",
                  "{red:Needs 'and'}"
                ],
                [
                  "Good",
                  "{green:Few or none}",
                  "{green:One clear job}"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Low-Cohesion Smell",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`Utils`, `Manager`, `Helper` classes",
                "They grow ==unrelated methods== over time",
                "Name needs 'and'? **Split it**"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "==Low coupling== outside, ==high cohesion== inside. One change should touch one place."
            },
            {
              "type": "sidebox",
              "title": "Interview Point",
              "items": [
                "**Coupling vs cohesion?** Between modules vs inside one",
                "**Test for coupling?** Change A, count modules that must change",
                "**Spot low cohesion?** Job needs 'and', or a Utils class"
              ],
              "ink": "orange"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Types of Coupling",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Types of Coupling",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Worst: Reaching In",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "{red:Content} (worst): reads or edits another module's ==internals==",
                "Private state access, reflection hacks",
                "{orange:Common}: modules share ==global mutable state==",
                "Any change can break **any reader**"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Flags and Fat Objects",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Type",
                "Smell",
                "Fix"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "{purple:Control}",
                  "caller passes a flag: `render(true)`",
                  "separate methods, or ==polymorphism=="
                ],
                [
                  "{blue:Stamp}",
                  "whole object, one field needed",
                  "pass the field, or a ==narrow interface=="
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Best: Data and Message",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "{green:Data} (best): only the ==primitive arguments== it needs",
                "{green:Message}: events; sender has ==no knowledge of receiver==, even looser"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Content",
                    "ink": "red"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Common",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Control",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Stamp",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Data",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Message",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Ladder",
              "text": "Worst to best: content, common, control, stamp, data, message. Pass ==only what is needed==."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "High Cohesion and the Law of Demeter",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "High Cohesion and the Law of Demeter",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Cohesion levels",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Level",
                "Parts grouped by"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "{green:Functional}",
                  "one well-defined task (best)"
                ],
                [
                  "Sequential",
                  "output of one feeds the next"
                ],
                [
                  "Communicational",
                  "same input data"
                ],
                [
                  "Logical",
                  "same category, chosen by a flag"
                ],
                [
                  "{red:Coincidental}",
                  "random grouping (worst)"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 0
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Cohesion = ==Single Responsibility Principle== at module level",
                "High cohesion = ==one reason to change=="
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Law of Demeter",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "A method may call only: **itself**, its **parameters**",
                "Objects it **creates**, its direct **fields**",
                "Smell: ==train-wreck== chains of getters"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "java",
              "lines": [
                "order.getCustomer().getAddress().getCity(); // ask",
                "order.shippingCity(); // tell, delegates"
              ],
              "note": "fix: tell, don't ask"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Trade-off",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Cost: more thin ==delegating methods==",
                "Don't wrap plain data structures",
                "Don't wrap fluent builders"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "One dot per call",
              "text": "Talk to friends only. A chain of three getters means the caller knows too much."
            },
            {
              "type": "sidebox",
              "title": "Interview Point",
              "items": [
                "**Worst cohesion?** Coincidental: unrelated methods, like a Utils class",
                "**Demeter fix?** Add `order.shippingCity()`; Order delegates",
                "**When ignore Demeter?** Plain data and fluent builders"
              ],
              "ink": "purple"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Composition over Inheritance and Dependency Injection",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Composition over Inheritance and Dependency Injection",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Inheritance vs Composition",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Inheritance is the ==tightest class coupling==: the subclass depends on the parent's implementation",
                "**Fragile base class**: a parent change silently breaks subclasses",
                "Composition: hold a collaborator as a field and ==delegate== to it"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Inheritance",
                "Composition"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Relation",
                  "is-a",
                  "has-a"
                ],
                [
                  "Depends on",
                  "parent's internals",
                  "an interface"
                ],
                [
                  "Swap at runtime",
                  "{red:no}",
                  "{green:yes}"
                ],
                [
                  "Testing",
                  "needs real parent",
                  "fakes"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 3
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flowchart",
              "spec": {
                "rows": [
                  [
                    "q"
                  ],
                  [
                    "a",
                    "b"
                  ]
                ],
                "nodes": {
                  "q": {
                    "text": "True is-a with Liskov guarantee?",
                    "shape": "diamond"
                  },
                  "a": {
                    "text": "Inherit",
                    "shape": "box",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  "b": {
                    "text": "Compose behind an interface",
                    "shape": "box",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  }
                },
                "edges": [
                  {
                    "from": "q",
                    "to": "a",
                    "label": "yes"
                  },
                  {
                    "from": "q",
                    "to": "b",
                    "label": "no"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Dependency Injection",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "A class ==receives== its dependencies instead of building them",
                "No `new Mailer()` inside the class"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "class Signup:",
                "    def __init__(self, mailer):",
                "        self.mailer = mailer",
                "    def run(self, user):",
                "        self.mailer.send(user)",
                "Signup(FakeMailer())  # in a test"
              ],
              "note": "constructor injection"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Style",
                "Use it"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "**Constructor**",
                  "{green:default}: immutable, explicit"
                ],
                [
                  "**Setter**",
                  "optional dependencies only"
                ],
                [
                  "Service locator, hidden global",
                  "{red:avoid}: hides dependencies"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Prefer ==composition + constructor injection==. Inherit only for a true is-a."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "How SOLID and Patterns Serve Low Coupling",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "How SOLID and Patterns Serve Low Coupling",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. SOLID: depend on abstractions",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "High-level code",
                    "sub": "owns the interface",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Abstraction",
                    "sub": "e.g. `Notifier`",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Low-level detail",
                    "sub": "implements it",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Dependency Inversion==: high-level code depends on an abstraction **it owns**",
                "Details (SMTP, SMS) implement that interface, not the reverse",
                "==Open/Closed==: extend via **new implementations**, no edits to old code",
                "==Interface Segregation==: small role interfaces avoid {red:stamp coupling}"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Patterns that cut coupling",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Pattern",
                "Removes",
                "Coupling gained"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "**Strategy / State**",
                  "`if/else` on a flag",
                  "swappable object"
                ],
                [
                  "**Factory**",
                  "`new Concrete()` calls",
                  "caller sees interface"
                ],
                [
                  "**Observer / Event bus**",
                  "publisher knows subscribers",
                  "{green:message} coupling"
                ],
                [
                  "**Facade / Adapter**",
                  "subsystem details",
                  "one narrow entry point"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Strategy and State replace {red:control-coupling} flags like `render(true)`",
                "Publisher just emits an event; it has ==no idea== who listens"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Trade-off: don't over-abstract",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Too many interfaces and indirection hurt ==readability==",
                "Add an abstraction only where **change** or **testing** demands it",
                "One implementation, no test need, no expected change: keep it concrete"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Every pattern buys ==looser coupling== with extra indirection. Pay only where change or testing needs it."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
